research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-33-{"id":"cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf","https://www.cs.uaf.edu/~maxwell/AY2007/math641/Measure.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT licenses countable nullity, and the UAF notes give the compact finite-subcover length argument for intervals. The local witness Q intersect [0,1] combines them to separate nullity from finite-cover content zero.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-34-{"id":"cex-meager-set-of-full-measure","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Meager_set"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics states that a meager subset of the real line can have full Lebesgue measure and that residual null sets exist. The local proof constructs such a decomposition explicitly from interval covers of the rationals.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"cex-cantor-point-that-is-not-an-endpoint","statement":"ai-generated","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"trivial","urls":[],"rationale":"This is a positive bespoke-witness determination: the item singles out one quarter rather than citing a named result. Its unique alternating 0,2 ternary sequence is not eventually constant, whereas every removed-gap endpoint has an eventually constant permitted expansion, so the witness is verified directly.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"cex-irrationals-are-not-f-sigma","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps/6.8.E%3A_Problems_on_Baire_Categories_and_Linear_Maps"],"rationale":"Zakon gives exactly that the rationals are not G-delta; complementation gives exactly that the irrationals are not F-sigma, while the same exercise records their residual G-delta form.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-37-{"id":"def-continuity-real","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.01%3A_Basic_Definitions"],"rationale":"Zakon gives the same relative epsilon-delta definition on a subset. The local definition additionally packages the function-limit equivalence at limit points and the automatic isolated-point case.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl:38:{"id":"thm-sequential-criterion-for-continuity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/"],"rationale":"Lebl presents the sequential criterion for continuity. The local statement keeps arbitrary subdomains and records the countable-choice cost of the converse, so it is a convention-aware adaptation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-39-{"id":"thm-algebra-of-continuous-functions","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The MIT notes list sums, products, quotients, composites, and polynomial continuity as the standard continuity algebra. The local theorem bundles absolute value, max, and min and expands epsilon-delta proofs in its dependency vocabulary.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"thm-composition-of-continuous-functions","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The MIT notes state continuity of composite maps. The local statement has the same domain and pointwise hypotheses and contrasts them with punctured function limits; the proof is the standard epsilon-delta substitution.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-41-{"id":"thm-continuity-preimage-characterisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Mathematical_Logic_and_Proof/An_Introduction_to_Proof_via_Inquiry-Based_Learning_%28Ernst%29/08%3A_New_Page/8.5%3A_Continuous_Real_Functions","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that continuity is equivalent to open preimages, with the relative-domain trace convention. The local item adds the dual closed-set form and proves both directions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-42-{"id":"thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"Both sources state that the continuous image of a compact set is compact. The local proof is an altered, choice-conscious open-cover argument, with the empty image handled explicitly before the nonempty finite-subcover construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-43-{"id":"cor-boundedness-theorem-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Compact_space"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics states that every real-valued continuous function on a compact space is bounded. The local corollary derives this immediately from compact image and Heine-Borel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
