research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-82-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-83-[L4] A strictly increasing index map satisfies $n_j \ge j$ ([[lem-index-map-grows]], [[def-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-84-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-85-[L5] Archimedean property in reciprocal form: for every real $\eta > 0$ there is a natural $n \ge 1$ with $1/n < \eta$; and $0 < s \le t$ implies $1/t \le 1/s$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[thm-of-archimedean]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-86-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md:87:[L6] Sequential criterion, the choice-free direction: if $f$ is continuous at $p \in K$ and $(z_j)$ has terms in $K$ with $z_j \to p$, then $f(z_j) \to f(p)$ ([[thm-sequential-criterion-for-continuity]], [[def-continuity-real]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-88-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-89-[L7] Triangle inequality and absolute value: $|u + v| \le |u| + |v|$, $|{-u}| = |u|$, $|u| \ge 0$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]], [[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-90-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/thm-heine-cantor-r.md-91-[L8] Convergence of real sequences is tested at rational $\varepsilon > 0$, and below every positive real lies a positive rational, so the test may equally be run at every real $\varepsilon > 0$ ([[def-real-limit]], [[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]).
