research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246584- {"id":"def-continuity-real","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/04%3A_Function_Limits_and_Continuity/4.01%3A_Basic_Definitions"],"rationale":"Zakon gives the same relative epsilon-delta definition on a subset. The local definition additionally packages the function-limit equivalence at limit points and the automatic isolated-point case.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log:246585: {"id":"thm-sequential-criterion-for-continuity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/"],"rationale":"Lebl presents the sequential criterion for continuity. The local statement keeps arbitrary subdomains and records the countable-choice cost of the converse, so it is a convention-aware adaptation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246586- {"id":"thm-algebra-of-continuous-functions","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The MIT notes list sums, products, quotients, composites, and polynomial continuity as the standard continuity algebra. The local theorem bundles absolute value, max, and min and expands epsilon-delta proofs in its dependency vocabulary.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246587- {"id":"thm-composition-of-continuous-functions","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The MIT notes state continuity of composite maps. The local statement has the same domain and pointwise hypotheses and contrasts them with punctured function limits; the proof is the standard epsilon-delta substitution.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246588- {"id":"thm-continuity-preimage-characterisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Mathematical_Logic_and_Proof/An_Introduction_to_Proof_via_Inquiry-Based_Learning_%28Ernst%29/08%3A_New_Page/8.5%3A_Continuous_Real_Functions","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"The sources state that continuity is equivalent to open preimages, with the relative-domain trace convention. The local item adds the dual closed-set form and proves both directions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246589--{"id":"thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"Both sources state that the continuous image of a compact set is compact. The local proof is an altered, choice-conscious open-cover argument; its current empty-set omission is separately proposed for repair.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-246590-+{"id":"thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"Both sources state that the continuous image of a compact set is compact. The local proof is an altered, choice-conscious open-cover argument, with the empty image handled explicitly before the nonempty finite-subcover construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
