research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-248433- 
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-248434- [L5] Convergence of a real sequence: $x_k \to x$ when for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with $|x_k - x| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$; below every positive real lies a positive rational, so the test may equally be run at every real $\varepsilon > 0$ ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]], [[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]).
