research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log:251150:-[L4] Heine criterion for limits: at a limit point $c$ of $A$, $\lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L$ holds if and only if $f(x_k) \to L$ for every sequence $(x_k)$ with $x_k \in A$, $x_k \ne c$ for every $k$, and $x_k \to c$. The direction from the limit to sequences is a theorem of ZF; the converse uses the axiom of countable choice exactly once ([[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]], [[def-countable-choice]], [[rem-heine-criterion-choice-cost]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log:251151:+[L4] Heine criterion for limits: at a limit point $c$ of $A$, $\lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L$ holds if and only if $f(x_k) \to L$ for every sequence $(x_k)$ with $x_k \in A$, $x_k \ne c$ for every $k$, and $x_k \to c$. The direction from the limit to sequences is a theorem of ZF; the converse uses the axiom of countable choice exactly once ([[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]], [[def-countable-choice]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-251152- 
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-251153- [L5] Convergence of a real sequence: $x_k \to x$ when for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K$ with $|x_k - x| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$; below every positive real lies a positive rational, so the test may equally be run at every real $\varepsilon > 0$ ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]], [[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]).
