research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-252001- {"id":"cex-meager-set-of-full-measure","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Meager_set"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics states that a meager subset of the real line can have full Lebesgue measure and that residual null sets exist. The local proof constructs such a decomposition explicitly from interval covers of the rationals.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
