research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-290863-+{"id":"thm-continuous-image-of-a-compact-set-r","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Introduction_to_Real_Analysis_%28Trench%29/08%3A_Metric_Spaces/8.00%3A_Introduction_to_Metric_Spaces","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.100/100B.S1-Lects.html"],"rationale":"Both sources state that the continuous image of a compact set is compact. The local proof is an altered, choice-conscious open-cover argument, with the empty image handled explicitly before the nonempty finite-subcover construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
